// generated by tools/make-patch.js from README.txt - do not edit
const PATCHNOTES=[["0.83","Floor 25: the level label in the top left says Castle (it said the underlying cave theme), and gravity in the castle is now normal instead of a quarter of normal, so jumps are no longer floaty. 0.84 - Floor 25: the Skyfall Warden boss is no longer upside down (talons hang below, head on top). 0.85 - City floors: the shop, library and arcade doors can no longer be wiped out by alleys or by rubble on ruined cities, so every city floor has an enterable shop (and library). Shops on alien cities now have the green sign on the door like the arcade and library. 0.86 - Shops: the SALE sticker on special deals now shows all four letters (the L was missing). 0.87 - Shops: the power items on the shelves (Second Opinion, Plated Vest and others) no longer flicker with lines while you move; overlapping flat faces are pushed apart by a tiny amount, so the designs look the same. 0.88 - Plated Vest is capped at 6 copies. Heart Overflow description shortened. The Tab menu with lots of powers now lays them out in columns across the full width (with a visible thin scrollbar), so long lists are no longer cut off."],["0.82","Singleplayer: when an enemy kills you, the results screen shows its name, health, damage, speed and traits, plus a small map with you and the killer marked (flashing red ring). Settings > Controls has a new Crosshair editor: line length, gap, thickness, center dot, circle, opacity, color, outline and T shape, with live previews, saved automatically."],["0.81","New title: Withered (a Rare loot box title)."],["0.80","Power names use proper capitalization everywhere (Phase Step, Gravity Well, Frag Grenade, Quick Hands and so on)."],["0.79","Hearts are no longer wasted: at full health you walk over them and they stay. New regular power Heart overflow: a heart eaten at full health gives +2 Overhealth (max 20; with Overheal too, the max is 40). Messiah now lasts 8 seconds instead of 5."],["0.78","Multiplayer: a player's equipped title now shows on their profile card in the lobby (it was only sent during matches before). The game music is 25% quieter; the Music slider keeps its range, so its 100% is the new, quieter level."],["0.77","Air Hockey multiplayer: the host can now move to the Spectators and watch. The first player then runs the table for the match."],["0.76","Game mode names now use proper capitalization everywhere (Battle Royale, Capture the Flag, Team Deathmatch, Bomb Defusal, Air Hockey and so on)."],["0.75","Arms Race: a kill no longer swaps your gun mid-round; the new gun arrives with the next round (a feed line tells you which). Battle royale and One in the Chamber: after you are eliminated the kill replay now ends and you can spectate the remaining players (Q / E or the mouse buttons to switch); before, the replay looped forever."],["0.74","Floor 25: fixed the lab doorway staying blocked after beating the Warden. A glowing trim strip ran straight across the open door at head height and was solid; it now stops at the doorway."],["0.73","Desktop: closing the game now makes sure every game process ends (cleans up Steam, Discord and the lobby server, then force-exits after 1.5 seconds), to stop leftover ghost windows in Alt-Tab."],["0.72","Profiles: a player's equipped title now shows in front of their name on their profile card (lobby click and your own preview)."],["0.71","Title screen: click the version number in the bottom left to open the patch notes (from the readme). It shows what changed since the version you were on before your last update, with a button to show every version."],["0.70","Arena machine: removed the long help text from the fullscreen top bar so the bar is slim."],["0.69","Arcade: the other machines have plain black screens. Playing Arena now shows a first-person view of you at the machine with the game running on its monitor; Alt+Enter (or the Fullscreen button) switches to the full-window view and back."],["0.68","Arena machine: fixed the game's own mount lines (drive written as \"C:\") not being resolved, which left Arena unable to start."],["0.67","Arcade Arena machine now uses the game's own DOSBox config (.conf files in its Steam folder: settings and launch commands) instead of guessed settings, keeps the game folder layout, and has a Log button to show what DOSBox is doing."],["0.66","Arcade: if The Elder Scrolls: Arena is installed in your Steam library, one arcade machine is switched on and runs it (DOSBox inside the game window; desktop app only; saved games are kept between visits; F12 leaves the machine)."],["0.65","Shop no-jumping sign is shorter and sits closer to the exit sign."],["0.64","The shop no-jumping sign now says \"NO JUMPING\" so it is obvious what it means."],["0.63","Added a silly \"no jumping\" sign on the shop wall next to the exit."],["0.62","You can no longer jump inside shops (your head went through the ceiling)."],["0.61","Custom Music now replaces the game's own music on levels that have it (Shops, Space station, Castle, Coliseum) so the two never play over each other. Those levels are marked with an asterisk in Settings > Audio > Custom Music."],["0.60","Settings > Audio now has a \"Custom Music\" submenu. The general YouTube link moved into it, and each level theme (Dungeon, Cavern, Lab, Crypt, Manor, Foundry, City, Mineshaft, Coliseum, Bandit hideout, Space station, Castle, Shops) can have its own YouTube link that plays instead of the general one on those levels."],["0.59","Debug mode: new \"Cutscene viewer\" button on the main menu under Sound tester. It plays the alien home world, the space elevator, the station crash (escape and left-behind), the ending and the coliseum boss entrance on their own, and returns to the list when each one ends."],["0.58","Cat Ears: the black part is larger so they read clearly as cat ears."],["0.57","New hat: Cat Ears (Uncommon), black ears with pink insides on a thin headband. Drops from loot boxes."],["0.56","New hat: Oni Horns (Rare), two stubby yellow ridged horns. It drops from loot boxes like the other hats."],["0.55","Reaper axe: the shaft now goes into the iron collar and comes out the other end cleanly (it no longer overlaps the collar faces)."],["0.54","Reaper axe: replaced the wide box at the top of the shaft (it stuck out of both sides with the shaft clipping through it) with a round mount ring."],["0.53","Reaper axe: the hand pegs no longer pass through the shaft (they are short stubs on each side), which fixes the overlapping/clipping look."],["0.52","Chest model: a bit more detail. Domed lid, plank grooves, iron plinth, corner brackets, back hinges, rivets on the gold straps, and a lock plate with a keyhole and hasp; cursed chests also get small iron spikes on the lid."],["0.51","Linux: BUILD.sh now builds a plain folder (dist/linux-unpacked) that can update itself, and PLAY-LINUX.sh prefers it; the AppImage is still available with ./BUILD.sh appimage. Single-file builds (AppImage, portable .exe) now show an \"update available\" box with a link to the download page instead of staying silent. Rebuild once with the new BUILD.sh to get the self-updating build."],["0.50","Reaper axe: removed the dark facet lines from the metal parts too (collar, spike, pommel, hand pegs)."],["0.49","Reaper axe handle: removed the many dark lines and stripes along the handle; it is now a smooth wooden shaft with two plain grip wraps."],["0.48","Fan gun damage +5% in singleplayer (multiplayer unchanged)."],["0.47","Scattergun damage +5%."],["0.46","The game now checks GitHub for a newer version when it starts and offers to install it (Update and restart / Later). It downloads the same checked game-files.zip as Updater.exe and backs up the old files. Turn it off with \"autoUpdate\": false in settings.json. Needs a game folder with resources\\app (not an .asar)."],["0.45","Added the MIT LICENSE, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt (credits for the orchestral samples, font, libraries and trademark notes), a GitHub README.md and .gitignore. Updates now come from GitHub: the new Updater.exe downloads the newest game files from the latest release of github.com/EffDeeArr/ad (checked by checksum, old files backed up) and works from any earlier version. Patch-to-*.exe files are no longer made."],["0.44","Fixed very low FPS with a frame cap above 60: vsync and the frame limiter are now only switched off when the cap is above the monitor refresh rate (before, any cap over 60 did it). The setting is re-checked at every start, so existing installs correct themselves after one extra restart."],["0.43","Startup in borderless fullscreen now waits for the window and game to finish loading before entering fullscreen (was done mid-load; reported to leave some PCs at very low FPS until the setting was toggled)."],["0.42","Super turret is now only 10% larger than the regular turret. Shots from both player turrets (and enemy turrets) now leave from the barrel tips. Shop power prices are now $40-80, and 2% of powers on the shelves are a SPECIAL DEAL at $30 with a SALE sticker."],["0.41","Super turret has its own look: gold armour plating, twin barrels with glowing muzzles, side ammo drums, a radar fin, a glowing base ring and a spinning ring of violet energy around the head, on top of being bigger than the regular turret."],["0.40","Two new powers. Afterimage (rare): after you take a hit you cannot be hurt again for 1 second (instead of the usual brief 0.2s). Thinned herd (regular, stacks up to 5): one less regular enemy on every floor per copy."],["0.39","Air hockey vs. the Monster now pays $50 for a win instead of $20."],["0.38","Shops (and libraries/arcades) now have a textured ceiling: speckled acoustic tiles in a grid with fluorescent light panels. It follows the ruined and alien looks on later floors. Works in both renderers."],["0.37","Enhanced mode: the shop shelves (and library bookshelves), the side of the counter and the cabinet now have much more detail: planked backs and sides with wood grain, grained shelf boards, metal brackets and nails, raised door panels with handles, a speckled top on the side counter, and a framed, grained cabinet."],["0.36","Alien shops: the wooden shelves, counter, side counter, cabinet and scratch-off stand are now pearl and violet with glowing trim and crystal tips."],["0.35","Alien floors: shops and libraries on floors 26+ are now alien (pearl-and-violet room, all signs and posters in alien script, an alien shopkeeper with a halo instead of a human cashier). Before this they showed the ruined look with leftover alien crystals, and the city spires showed through the shop ceiling."],["0.34","Alien city: roofs now sit flush on the buildings (the base slab matches the building footprint instead of overhanging and looking like it floats)."],["0.33","Alien city: every building now has a real 3D spire on top (stacked pearl tiers, a glowing ring floating around it and a glowing crystal tip), replacing the flat pointed shapes. Works in both renderers."],["0.32","Alien city: each building now has one large pointed roof over its whole frontage (taller for wider buildings) instead of a row of small spikes."],["0.31","Alien floors: the screen effect (light motes and violet vignette) is now much fainter. The alien city now matches the cutscene cities: pearl buildings with pointed roofs, no windows, and every building carries a sign in made-up alien script instead of English, so the only way to tell you can enter one is the green sign on its door."],["0.30","After the floor 25 boss falls and the science lab opens, a prototype alien teleporter stands inside: step into the ring and a short 3D cutscene shows the alien home world (floating pearl cities, light bridges, a ringed planet). Space skips it. Floors 26 and up are alien versions of every level theme: pearl-and-crystal walls with glowing veins, a floating-spire skyline, alien props (seed pods, crystal spires, stasis capsules, hover-pods in cities), drifting light motes, and no humans. Not tested on a real GPU or with audio."],["0.29","The game keeps its 0.x version style (0.29, 0.30, ...). package.json now stores it in the three-part form the build tools require (0.29.0, 0.30.0, ...); the title screen, patches and updater show it as 0.29. Gameplay is unchanged from 0.28."],["0.28","Cold snap model: rebuilt from pieces that only touch instead of three bars passing through each other, which removes the flickering/overlapping faces. Same shape and colors."],["0.27","Dungeon shop now only appears on floors with the Dungeon theme (not Lab, Foundry, Manor, Crypt, Cavern, City, Mineshaft, etc.)."],["0.26","Dungeon shop: about half of ordinary dungeon floors now have a small shop room built into the level: a table with 3 random powers for $50 each (press F next to it), a skull-masked shopkeeper behind it, and two little fires. Buying something makes the shopkeeper say \"It's dangerous to go alone! Take this\". Not on city, mineshaft, boss, special or multiplayer floors."],["0.25","Twin daggers deal 25% more damage in singleplayer."],["0.24","Floor 25: siege wave monsters now have 50% less health and damage than normal floor 25 monsters (was 25%)."],["0.23","Floor 25: closed the gap between the lab door steps and the lab floor (grass was visible through it)."],["0.22","Floor 25: the landing pad beside the lab is now a solid, thicker platform sunk into the ground (it looked like it was floating and its dark sides vanished at some angles)."],["0.21","Floor 25: the castle gate facing the lab is now open and the other gate is shut (the keep moved to the north end); the lab entrance has steps up to it and is sealed by a force field until the waves and the Skyfall Warden are defeated."],["0.20","Floor 25: fixed the flickering stripes on the castle wall beside the gates (two overlapping wall faces were fighting each other)."],["0.19","Floor 25 is now The Siege: a small stone castle with stairs up to the ramparts. Survive 5 waves of weak monsters (25% less health and damage, no modifiers), walk to the alien science lab, and the Skyfall Warden (a huge mecha bird that drops bombs, fires bolt fans and dives every ~6 seconds) attacks. New real-instrument orchestral battle theme. Textures on this map are 256x256 (the engine now supports 256px textures in both renderers)."],["0.18","Stuck rescue hardened: it now also fixes a broken (non-numeric) player position, skips remembered safe spots that have since become blocked, and searches fresh if a rescue does not hold."],["0.17","Stuck rescue for every mode and floor: if you are inside something for over a second, or hold a movement key for 2.5 seconds while boxed in on every side, you are teleported back to the last safe spot (or the nearest open one)."],["0.16","Floor 15: respawning after a fall now searches for a valid free spot near the checkpoint (not inside a wall or on a jump pad) and widens the search if you get put back repeatedly, so you can no longer end up unable to move."],["0.15","Air hockey: the field is split into four invisible quadrants; a puck that stays in one for 6 straight seconds resets to the middle. Puck hit sounds are rate-limited so they no longer stack into a loud noise."],["0.14","Air hockey: if the puck gets pinned in a corner/wall on the monster's side, it is now kicked back toward the middle instead of being pushed there forever."],["0.13","DEFLECT text raised; the ready icon is grey during the cooldown and fills with blue from the bottom as it recovers."],["0.12","Deflect cues: your melee weapon glows blue and DEFLECT shows at the bottom middle while it is active; a small blue icon of your melee weapon shows there when it is ready again."],["0.11","Blink dash now carries you over pits when you have climbing hooks. Melee blocking now cuts damage taken by 50% (was 33%)."],["0.6","Ashen Knight fires 50% more projectiles in his second phase. New melee-only power \"Deflect\": while blocking, enemy shots are reflected at enemies for the shot's damage (3 s per block, then 6 s cooldown, cannot stack, never offered to gun builds)."]];
